<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Northern Cape</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Northern Cape is the largest province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a> by area and the least populous, created in 1994 from the north-western part of the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-province">Cape Province</a>. Its capital is <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kimberley">Kimberley</a>, centre of the diamond rush of the 1870s. Much of it is semi-desert, including Namaqualand and parts of the Kalahari, and it has large Afrikaans-speaking and Tswana populations.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/northern-cape.jpg" alt="Northern Cape" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Graham Maclachlan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diamondfields,_South_Africa_-_panoramio_(5).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
